---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'

const groups = [
  {
    heading: 'Prose',
    items: [
      { name: 'Novel', starts: 'Prologue (off), Chapter 1 with Scene 1, Epilogue (off)', label: 'Chapter', front: 'Manuscript Format, Paperback, Ebook', exports: 'Manuscript, Paperback, Proof, EPUB' },
      { name: 'Non-Fiction', starts: 'Chapter 1 with Section 1', label: 'Chapter (numbered)', front: 'Manuscript Format, Paperback, Ebook', exports: 'Manuscript, Paperback, Proof, EPUB' },
      { name: 'Short Story / Essay', starts: 'Scene 1, no chapters', label: 'Section', front: 'Manuscript Format, Paperback, Ebook', exports: 'Manuscript, EPUB' },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: "Children's books",
    items: [
      { name: "Children's Book (Square)", starts: 'Page 1', label: 'Page', front: 'Manuscript Format, Paperback', exports: "Children's Book 8.5″ × 8.5″" },
      { name: "Children's Book (Portrait)", starts: 'Page 1', label: 'Page', front: 'Manuscript Format, Paperback', exports: "Children's Book 8.5″ × 11″" },
      { name: "Children's Book (Landscape)", starts: 'Page 1', label: 'Page', front: 'Manuscript Format, Paperback', exports: "Children's Book 11″ × 8.5″" },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Academic',
    items: [
      { name: 'Academic Paper (APA 7th)', starts: 'An empty manuscript', label: 'Section', front: 'Manuscript Format', exports: 'APA 7th (DOCX, PDF)' },
      { name: 'Academic Paper (MLA 9th)', starts: 'An empty manuscript', label: 'Section', front: 'Manuscript Format', exports: 'MLA 9th (DOCX, PDF)' },
      { name: 'Essay (Chicago 17th)', starts: 'An empty manuscript', label: 'Section', front: 'Manuscript Format', exports: 'Chicago 17th (DOCX, PDF)' },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Scripts',
    items: [
      { name: 'Screenplay', starts: 'Act One, Two and Three, each with Scene 1', label: 'Act', front: 'Screenplay', exports: 'Screenplay PDF, Fountain' },
      { name: 'TV Script', starts: 'Cold Open, Act One, Act Two, Tag', label: 'Act', front: 'TV Script', exports: 'Screenplay PDF, Fountain' },
      { name: 'Documentary Script', starts: 'Segment 1 and 2, each with Scene 1', label: 'Segment', front: 'TV Script', exports: 'Documentary PDF, Fountain' },
      { name: 'Stage Play (US)', starts: 'Act One and Two, each with Scene 1', label: 'Act', front: 'Manuscript Format', exports: 'Stage Play (US) PDF' },
      { name: 'Stage Play (UK)', starts: 'Act One and Two, each with Scene 1', label: 'Act', front: 'Manuscript Format', exports: 'Stage Play UK PDF' },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Other',
    items: [
      { name: 'Blank', starts: 'An empty manuscript', label: 'Chapter', front: 'All five folders', exports: 'Any' },
    ],
  },
]
---
<DocsLayout title="Project Templates" description="The 15 project types in Ravenburst and what each one sets up for you.">
  <h1>Project Templates</h1>
  <p class="lede">When you create a project you choose what kind of work it is. That sets up a starting structure, the word used for chapters, the line spacing, and front matter for the formats you're likely to export.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>A template is only a starting point. You can add, rename and reorder anything afterwards, and any project can be exported to any format in the <a href="/docs/compile-options">Compile</a> dialog.</p>
  </div>

  {groups.map((g) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{g.heading}</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Template</th><th>Starts with</th><th>Chapters are called</th><th>Front matter folders</th><th>Made for</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {g.items.map((t) => (
              <tr><td><strong>{t.name}</strong></td><td>{t.starts}</td><td>{t.label}</td><td>{t.front}</td><td>{t.exports}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Also set by the template</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Line spacing:</strong> double for prose, children's books and academic work (standard submission format); single for scripts and plays; 1.5 for Blank.</li>
    <li><strong>Back matter:</strong> Novel, Non-Fiction and Short Story start with an <em>About the Author</em> page. Other types start with none, and you can add pages yourself.</li>
    <li><strong>Templates:</strong> starter documents in the Templates section, such as <em>Blank Scene</em>, <em>Scene with Synopsis Block</em>, <em>Chapter Opening</em>, <em>Screenplay Scene</em>, <em>TV Scene</em> and <em>Reference Note</em>, depending on the type. See <a href="/docs/navigator#templates">Templates</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The Novel's Prologue and Epilogue start switched off, marked “(off)” above. Tick <strong>Include in Final Draft</strong> to write in them and compile them, or ignore them if your book doesn't need them.</p>
</DocsLayout>
